  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Hi",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I am very sorry to report that I have just discovered a memory leak in",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "the ECM code. Actually, not in the ECM code, but in a library that ECM",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "depends on.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The problem lies in the owlapi library, which I added to Fedora. Every",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "time a validation is performed, a new Ontology idenfier is autogenerated",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "by OWLAPI, and stored in a static map. This information is never used,",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "in fact it is sufficiently protected to prevent if from ever being used.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "But still, perform enough validations, and your system will choke.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I have contacted the OWLAPI mailing list with the bug. As for Fedora, we",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "could either just keep going for now, or we could perform our own fix.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The bug:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The IRI class contain the following static map",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "private static Map<String, String> prefixCache = new HashMap<String,String>();",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This bit of the constructor is the ONLY use of this map",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "String cached = prefixCache.get(prefix);",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "if (cached == null) {",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "prefixCache.put(prefix, prefix);",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "}",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "else {",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "prefix = cached;",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "}",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For a longrunning process, I have seen the map grow to 553 MB",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
